    {
      "title": "Delhi HC seeks FSSAI’s stand in PIL case against non-dairy, analogue paneer",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/delhi-high-court-seeks-fssai-stand-on-pil-against-non-dairy-analogous-paneer/article71583002.ece",
      "description": "Gujarat, Punjab, Chhattisgarh and Maharashtra have already taken steps against non-dairy paneer, the plea says, seeking directions to prevent the supply of dairy analogue paneer in the national capital",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-14T17:44:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delhi HC seeks replies on plea against non-dairy products sold as paneer",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-hc-seeks-replies-on-plea-against-non-dairy-products-sold-as-paneer-126101401289_1.html",
      "description": "The PIL seeks inspections and action against non-dairy substitutes sold as paneer without disclosure. The Delhi High Court gave authorities six weeks to respond to the plea",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-14T15:14:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delhi HC seeks FSSAI stand on PIL against non-dairy, analogous 'paneer'",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-hc-seeks-fssai-stand-on-pil-against-non-dairy-analogous-paneer-126101400598_1.html",
      "description": "The Delhi High Court on Wednesday sought the stand of the FSSAI, the Centre and the city government on a PIL raising concerns over the sale of dairy analogue/non-dairy products as 'paneer' to unsuspecting consumers.\nThe petitioners contended that while paneer is a standardised dairy product under the food safety regime, a non-dairy, analogue product contains non-milk ingredients and lacks the same nutritional value.\nA bench of acting Chief Justice Nitin W Sambre and Justice Sanjay Singh issued notices to the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI), the Centre and the Delhi government on the petition filed by Ridhima Singh and Avlokiteshwar Padmapani Sidharth, and asked them to file their replies within six weeks.\nThe petitioners contended that a person consuming a paneer-based product in a hotel or a restaurant has no means to know whether the dish is prepared using actual paneer or a dairy analogue.\nThey sought urgent directions from the court in view of the festive .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-14T08:46:05"
    }
  ]
